(272,'4f4072e0-1bb1-47e9-98fa-4f1a21e3f787',NULL,'registered','1782990174716-7506','assistant','THOUGHT: My apologies! The user corrected me, they want to know the age of the main character, Amirmohammad, not the principal. I need to:\n\n1.  **Apologize and correct:** Acknowledge the misunderstanding and apologize for it.\n2.  **Shift focus to Amirmohammad:** Re-state the question specifically for Amirmohammad.\n3.  **Consider Amirmohammad\'s characteristics:** He\'s smart, brave, a student in an old school in Yazd, part of a trio solving a mystery about a lost sports cup.\n4.  **Brainstorm age ranges for a young detective:**\n    *   Very young (7-9): Might be a bit too young for serious detective work, though charming.\n    *   Middle primary (10-12): Perfect for school-based mysteries, old enough to be resourceful but still a kid. This fits the \"6-10\" and \"10-12\" age modules in the persona for child users.\n    *   Early teen (13-14): Also good, but might shift the tone slightly from \"school mystery\" to \"teen mystery.\"\n5.  **Propose an age range:** A range like 10-12 or 11-13 seems ideal for a character who is smart, brave, and leading a detective team in a school setting. This age also fits well with the idea of participating in school sports like track, darts, and soccer.\n6.  **Explain the reasoning:** Why this age fits his personality (smart, brave, leader) and the story (school setting, sports competition).\n7.  **Engage the user:** Ask for their thoughts or confirmation.\n\nLet\'s aim for an age that makes him resourceful but still distinctly a *child* protagonist, which aligns with the overall prompt\'s focus on younger audiences. 11-12 years old feels right.','gemini-2.5-flash',5423,'{\"promptTokenCount\":10137,\"candidatesTokenCount\":743,\"totalTokenCount\":10880,\"cachedContentTokenCount\":8981,\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":10137}],\"cacheTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":8981}],\"serviceTier\":\"standard\"}',NULL,'plan_allowed','2026-07-03 05:04:48'),
